  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - This notice indicates that the proposed development would comply with conditions MA.2 of Schedule 2 Part 3 Class M of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 2015 (as amended) (\"the GPDO\"). \nIt is a requirement of condition MA.2(5) of the GPDO that the development must be completed within a period of 3 years starting with the prior approval date. \nIt is a requirement of condition M.A2(6) of the GPDO that any building permitted to be used as a dwellinghouse by virtue of Class MA is to remain in use as a dwellinghouse within the meaning of Class C3 of Schedule 1 to the Use Classes Order and for no other purpose, except to the extent that the other purpose is ancillary to the use as a dwellinghouse.\nIt is a requirement of paragraph W(12) of the GPDO that the development is carried out in accordance with the details provided in the application unless the developer and the local planning authority agree in writing.",
    "Condition : 2 - Prior to the commencement of above ground works (excluding demolition), details of the siting, design and materials of refuse and recycling storage to serve the development shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The refuse storage facilities shall be provided in accordance with the approved details prior to occupation of the development, and shall be retained thereafter.\nReason: In the interests of amenity and hygiene, in accordance with Council policy LP1 and LP2 of the Local Plan coupled with the requirements of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Condition : 3 - Finished floor levels for bedrooms 1 and 2 (as identified in Proposed Floor Plans, ref: 2478_PA_103 Rev A) shall be set no lower than 4.4 metres Above Ordnance Datum (mAOD), in line with section 4.11 of the submitted Flood Risk Assessment (reference: AEG7182_SW11_Battersea_01).\nThis mitigation measure shall be fully implemented prior to occupation and\nsubsequently in accordance with the scheme�s timing/phasing arrangement. The measure detailed above shall be retained and maintained thereafter throughout the lifetime of the development.\nReasons: To reduce the risk of flooding to the development and occupants. The ground floor is the lowest floor level that will have sleeping accommodation, according to the submitted documentation. To comply with Policy LP12 Water and Flooding on the Wandsworth Local Plan\n(2023).",
    "Condition : 4 - INFORMATIVE: You are advised that this application is made under Class MA, Part 3, Schedule 2 of the Town and Country (General Permitted Development) (Amendment) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) only and does not override any such planning conditions or associated legal agreements that relate to the site, buildings or uses."
  ],
